# The ledger of `web/chain`: what Echo's middleware, Gin's and chi's handler
# chains and Flask's request hooks let a program run around a route's
# handler, one block per capability, and what Rebel answers. Rust's standard
# library holds no web framework, so its lines are `-`.

capability chain/every  a step every route runs, in the order the steps were added
  heroes  web/chain.add_step, web.Router.steps
  go      echo.Echo.Use, gin.Engine.Use, chi.Router.Use, chi.Chain
  rust    -
  python  flask.Flask.before_request, flask.Flask.after_request
  note    run after the router found the route, as Echo's `Use` (its `Pre`, before the routing, is `web.before` in the program's loop); a request no route takes runs these steps too, then `web.not_routed`'s answer, as Echo's `Use` wraps its not-found handler, so a log line counts it

capability chain/group  a step every route of a group runs
  heroes  web/chain.add_step, web.Route.steps, web.mount
  go      echo.Group.Use, gin.RouterGroup.Use, chi.Router.Group, chi.Router.Route
  rust    -
  python  flask.Blueprint.before_request, flask.Blueprint.after_request
  note    added to the group's router before `web.mount` takes its routes and travelling with them, outermost group first; a step a group gains after the mount stays the group's, as a route it gains does

capability chain/route  a step one route runs after its groups'
  heroes  web/chain.add_route_step, web.Route.steps
  go      echo.Echo.Add's middleware, echo.Echo.GET's middleware, chi.Router.With, gin.RouterGroup.Handle's handlers
  rust    -
  python  -
  note    by the route's name, so every method sharing that name runs it

capability chain/next  a step going on to the next, or answering without going on, its work after the rest seeing the response
  heroes  web/chain.proceed, web/chain.Next
  go      echo.MiddlewareFunc, echo.HandlerFunc, gin.Context.Next, gin.Context.Abort, gin.Context.IsAborted, gin.HandlersChain
  rust    -
  python  -
  note    the `next` is data, `Next`, never a function returning a function that holds it, the language having no closure; a step goes on by calling `proceed` with the program's tables and the `Next` it was handed, and every step and answer is lent the program's state by `@`, so a step changes the state as a handler does

capability chain/bind  a route added and bound to the function that answers it
  heroes  web/chain.on
  go      echo.Echo.GET, echo.Echo.POST, echo.Echo.Add, gin.RouterGroup.GET, chi.Router.Get, net/http.ServeMux.HandleFunc
  rust    -
  python  flask.Flask.route, flask.Flask.add_url_rule
  note    the program keeps the function in its own table by the route's name, and the router the name alone, so nothing of the program's is held by the library

capability chain/dispatch  a request answered through its route's steps and handler
  heroes  web/chain.dispatch, web/chain.start, web/chain.Target
  go      echo.Echo.ServeHTTP, gin.Engine.ServeHTTP, chi.Mux.ServeHTTP
  rust    -
  python  flask.Flask.full_dispatch_request
  note    a name the program bound to no function aborts, a mistake in the program and never something a request can cause

capability chain/route-read  the route a step reads: its name, its groups, its parameters
  heroes  web/chain.found_of, web.Found
  go      echo.Context.Path, echo.Context.Param, gin.Context.FullPath, chi.RouteContext
  rust    -
  python  flask.Request.url_rule, flask.Request.endpoint

dropped  a context a step sets values in for the handler (Echo's `Context.Set`, Gin's `Context.Set`, Flask's `g`): the program's own state, lent by `@` to every step and answer, holds what a step finds
